1
00:00:49,070 --> 00:00:52,980
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:55,690
[Episode 17]

3
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:07,120
Fang.

4
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:09,539
Why are you doing this?

5
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:12,530
Things were going so well.
Why throw it all away?

6
00:01:12,930 --> 00:01:14,660
I've been so worried about you.

7
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:15,710
Tell me.

8
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:17,710
Tell me, what did Zhou ever do to you?

9
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:19,730
Everyone else who marries
and moves to Shanghai

10
00:01:19,730 --> 00:01:21,130
never wants to come back.

11
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:24,260
But why are you so... so stubborn?

12
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:26,460
Why can't you appreciate what you have?

13
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,970
What, are you possessed or something?

14
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,979
You'd better go back while you still can.

15
00:01:33,979 --> 00:01:35,210
Don't wait until he changes his mind

16
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:36,410
and you can't go back.

17
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,900
At least think about
what's best for the child.

18
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,760
How much is this book?

19
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:22,910
1.5 yuan.

20
00:02:23,450 --> 00:02:31,320
[Literary Fiction]

21
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:27,630
What about this one?

22
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:32,020
Isn't the price written on the back?

23
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,350
Bring me that one.

24
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:39,610
I want to take a look.

25
00:02:40,370 --> 00:02:41,020
Which one?

26
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,130
The one on top.

27
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:45,900
Up there, near the edge.

28
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:49,410
What, can't you tell up from down?

29
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:50,750
Can you understand a word I'm saying?

30
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:51,740
Up top!

31
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,780
The very top!

32
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:00,950
[Literary Fiction]

33
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:03,940
[Psoriasis Treatment and Prevention]

34
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:04,150
"Psoriasis Treatment and..."

35
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,560
Are you sick or something?

36
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,930
Why the hell did you bring me this book?

37
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:07,970
Who are you trying to insult?

38
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:09,240
Are you trying to piss me off?

39
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,360
Do you know who I am?

40
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:11,560
I do.

41
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:13,260
If you're buying a book,

42
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:14,400
you're a customer.

43
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,520
If you're not buying one,

44
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,430
then get out.

45
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:18,680
Who do you think you're talking to?

46
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,970
What's with that attitude?

47
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:21,630
What kind of attitude is that?

48
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,180
What kind of riffraff

49
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:24,579
do you hire around here?

50
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:25,190
to work for you?

51
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:25,970
I'm sorry.

52
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:27,030
-Have you no shame?
-Ma'am, sorry, sorry.

53
00:03:27,030 --> 00:03:28,410
You may have no shame, but I do.

54
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:28,970
All right, all right.

55
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:29,800
Don't you know

56
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,560
what you've done?

57
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:30,930
All right, ma'am.

58
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:32,690
-She's new here.
-You look so clean-cut,

59
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:33,780
but you're rotten to the core!

60
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:34,980
What did I do? Tell me.

61
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:38,780
You weren't ashamed to do it,

62
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:39,840
but I'm ashamed even to say it.

63
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,400
Tell me.

64
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,250
Do I really have to spell it out for you?

65
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:41,900
Say it.

66
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,000
You want me to say it, right?

67
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:50,860
Fine. Just you wait.

68
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,560
We'll see whether I say it or not.

69
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:54,320
I'll tell everyone about it!

70
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:55,750
How ridiculous.

71
00:03:57,590 --> 00:03:58,360
My gloves!

72
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:16,829
Poor Fang...

73
00:04:17,410 --> 00:04:20,810
She has no one to stand up for her
when things like this happen.

74
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:23,980
It's just not the same
without a man in the house.

75
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:26,480
I heard her husband
dumped her and divorced her.

76
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,890
He didn't even want the kid.

77
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:29,310
They say he married a local woman.

78
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,510
What?

79
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:32,110
I heard from Fang's neighbor

80
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:33,570
that she has someone else.

81
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:34,830
The guy is in Tiecheng.

82
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:36,810
Who is it?

83
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,130
Apparently,

84
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,340
she found herself a technician
at the boiler plant.

85
00:04:58,450 --> 00:05:00,110
Why are you going to Shanghai?

86
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:01,500
Will your dad even look after you?

87
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,300
He doesn't care about you at all.

88
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,120
I'm going back to Shanghai to find my dad.

89
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,750
Do you really have to go find your dad?

90
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:08,660
Even if you go to him,

91
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:10,160
he won't look after you.

92
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:13,690
Just stop it.

93
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:16,310
It's all because you were fooling around

94
00:05:16,310 --> 00:05:17,890
that you drove Dad away.

95
00:05:17,890 --> 00:05:19,330
I don't want to stay here.

96
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,270
What kind of godforsaken place is this?

97
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:23,530
I'm going back to Shanghai to find my dad.

98
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:24,890
Hao Jie.

99
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:27,000
Hao Jie.

100
00:05:29,810 --> 00:05:31,870
I work myself to the bone all day long.

101
00:05:32,150 --> 00:05:33,370
I sew clothes for people in the morning

102
00:05:33,370 --> 00:05:35,500
and stuff quilts with cotton at night.

103
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:37,800
You can't be so ungrateful.

104
00:05:38,830 --> 00:05:41,090
I'm going back to Shanghai to find my dad.

105
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:45,120
Mom, look! So much yummy food!

106
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:36,720
Liu Yang.

107
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:38,750
Liu Yang.

108
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,390
Did you guys hear that just now?

109
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:21,500
There was a huge bang. It was so loud.

110
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,500
Yeah, what happened?

111
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,130
They say the boiler room exploded.

112
00:07:24,130 --> 00:07:25,160
Did anyone get hurt?

113
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:26,290
Several people did.

114
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,960
Especially the technician,

115
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:28,830
Liu Weiguo.

116
00:07:28,830 --> 00:07:30,870
He was covered in soot
when they brought him out.

117
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,720
Then he must be in bad shape.

118
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:33,800
I'm telling you...

119
00:07:33,730 --> 00:07:37,050
[Emergency]

120
00:07:35,870 --> 00:07:37,250
Has Liu Weiguo's family arrived?

121
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:37,890
Not yet.

122
00:07:37,890 --> 00:07:38,770
Hurry up and get in touch with them.

123
00:07:38,770 --> 00:07:39,330
Okay.

124
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:29,060
Fang.

125
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:32,150
In my eyes,

126
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:35,350
you're prettier than that mannequin
behind the counter.

127
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:38,500
I won't be pretty when I get old.

128
00:08:39,370 --> 00:08:41,909
I might not even get to see you
when you're old.

129
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:53,820
Fang.

130
00:09:59,170 --> 00:10:00,030
I'm leaving.

131
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,300
You should go back.

132
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,510
I loved you.

133
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,820
I've never loved anyone else.

134
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:24,030
And I never will.

135
00:11:25,710 --> 00:11:31,370
[The end]

136
00:11:46,270 --> 00:11:49,240
♪ Cold and warm, when can they rest? ♪

137
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,910
[Door and Window Workshop]

138
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:53,360
♪ Looking back, how many autumns? ♪

139
00:11:54,270 --> 00:11:57,390
♪ Searched everywhere, yet lost instead ♪

140
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:58,530
Having a good day today?

141
00:11:58,530 --> 00:11:59,550
How could she not be happy?

142
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:01,760
♪ Did I get it or not? ♪

143
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:01,940
We found the hand.

144
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:04,200
This Wang Liye is a prime suspect.

145
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,270
He's been handed over
to the criminal investigation unit.

146
00:12:06,270 --> 00:12:07,440
Now Juan

147
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:08,900
can finally breathe easy.

148
00:12:10,050 --> 00:12:11,580
After all that work
for over half a month,

149
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:12,750
we finally got somewhere.

150
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:14,200
All that talk of gods and ghosts—

151
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,270
now it's all clear.

152
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:16,930
Someone did it deliberately.

153
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,050
But there's no evidence

154
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:20,540
that Wang Liye did it.

155
00:12:21,790 --> 00:12:23,120
That guy is so suspicious.

156
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:24,700
You can tell something's off about him.

157
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:26,530
He doesn't even have an alibi.

158
00:12:26,530 --> 00:12:27,340
If you had nothing to hide,

159
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:28,580
why would you run, huh?

160
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:29,820
And the way he talked,
all trembling and jittery.

161
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:32,020
It's definitely him. No doubt about it.

162
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,700
Even if he did run,

163
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,760
why would he leave the hand in the car?

164
00:12:37,250 --> 00:12:38,890
And the car was parked at a gas station.

165
00:12:38,890 --> 00:12:40,940
Wasn't he afraid someone would find it?

166
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,270
You're pretty thorough

167
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,640
for a household registration officer.

168
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:47,700
I've been reading detective novels
at home lately.

169
00:12:48,530 --> 00:12:50,320
Anyway, this case
isn't our problem anymore.

170
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,130
How could we handle a murder case?

171
00:12:52,130 --> 00:12:54,510
If you... if you set your mind
to committing a crime,

172
00:12:54,510 --> 00:12:55,750
you can exploit every loophole there is.

173
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:56,770
What can a beat cop like us

174
00:12:56,770 --> 00:12:57,820
do about it?

175
00:12:58,390 --> 00:13:01,050
Once we catch Wang Liye,
the truth will come out.

176
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:05,050
But what if Wang Liye didn't run?

177
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:06,500
What if he's dead?

178
00:13:24,270 --> 00:13:28,520
[Emergency]

179
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:58,080
I'll go to them and tell them I did it.

180
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:58,840
Go home.

181
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,010
What did they tell you?

182
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,320
Just say you don't know anything.

183
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,960
Say I told you to do it.

184
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:23,060
They're going to call the police.

185
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,320
Do you want to go to prison?

186
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:31,360
The department head
has known me for years.

187
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:34,200
He won't hold it against someone
who's dying.

188
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,210
If you go, you're done for.

189
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:43,820
How are we going to pay for it?

190
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,460
Where's the passbook?

191
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:32,090
I'll figure out the rest of the money.

192
00:15:34,050 --> 00:15:35,130
We'll find a way.
